# Disable browser caching for the hand-served JS/CSS in this no-bundler
# app. Discovered empirically during the 2026-09-05 UX pass (see
# .claude/plans/fancy-crafting-lark.md): with no Cache-Control header at
# all, browsers apply RFC 7234 heuristic freshness off Last-Modified, so
# an edited .js file can silently keep serving its PRE-edit body for
# hours — even across a plain reload — until the heuristic window
# expires. Since there's no build step / versioned filenames to bust
# this the normal way, disable caching for these two extensions outright
# rather than let every future session re-discover the same confusion.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(js|css)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
